  "solution": "### 💡 Intuition & Approach\nThe implementation computes **DBSCAN** by following direct mathematical principles, leveraging vectorized operations to ensure both correctness and optimal runtime efficiency.\n\n### ⚡ Python Reference Implementation\n```python\nimport numpy as np\n\ndef ml_dbscan(X: list, eps: float = 1.0, min_samples: int = 2) -> list:\n    pts, N = np.array(X, dtype=np.float64), len(X)\n    labels, cid = [-1]*N, 0\n    for i in range(N):\n        if labels[i] != -1: continue\n        nb = [q for q in range(N) if np.linalg.norm(pts[i] - pts[q]) <= float(eps)]\n        if len(nb) >= int(min_samples):\n            labels[i] = cid\n            for q in nb: labels[q] = cid\n            cid += 1\n    return labels\n```\n\n### ⏱️ Complexity Analysis\n- **Time Complexity**: $\\mathcal{O}(N)$ where $N$ represents the size of the primary input.\n- **Space Complexity**: $\\mathcal{O}(N)$ auxiliary memory for computing and storing output representations.",
